    <Label Name="Title" Style="GalleryTitle" Text="Gears" Pin="TopRight" OffsetX="16" OffsetY="16" WrapWidth="400" Backdrop="true" />
    <Label Name="Description" Style="GalleryText" Text="Drag the slider to turn the yellow gear. Its teeth push the green gear the other way, and the green gear pushes the purple one back the first way: every gear in a chain turns against its neighbors.\n\nThe yellow gear has 12 teeth and the green one 20. The yellow gear has made [spin / 3] turns, so the green one has made [12 / 20 * spin / 3]: a big gear turns slower than a small one, by exactly the ratio of their teeth. The purple gear, with 8 teeth, has made [12 / 8 * spin / 3] turns. Watch the white dots.\n\nThat is how a bicycle works. Pedal a 48-tooth chainring driving a 12-tooth sprocket and the back wheel spins four times for every turn of your feet." Pin="TopRight" OffsetX="16" OffsetY="64" WrapWidth="400" Backdrop="true">
      <Dependency Name="spin" />
    </Label>
